<title>USA: Prudential in policyholder settlement - attorney.</title>
<headline>Prudential in policyholder settlement - attorney.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prudential Insurance Co of America agreed to pay at least $410 million to settle lawsuits by policyholders claiming they were improperly sold life insurance policies, an attorney for the plaintiffs said.</p>
<p>Under the settlement, about 10.7 million policyholders are eligible to apply for restitution, Melvyn Weiss, one of the lead attorneys negotiating the settlement, said in a telephone conference call with reporters.</p>
</text>
